# scaling-timing.vrs: scaling D22 (tick budget with every scaled read running). The dev events.json holds sc-timing-a,
# sc-timing-b, sc-timing-c and sc-timing-d (tools/vrclient/fixtures/sc-timing-*.json: unit-watch's uw-timing-* waveLists
# of 12 then 6 CHAR_Spider_Forest, wave 2 after 60 s, at the pond (-1880, -1640) and 125 m north, east and south, each with
# the scaling block 2/true/2/1) and apo-test from fixtures/sc-apo-timing.json (apocalypse's D29 timing apo-test: 3
# hotspots x 10 roamers, max 30, horde 1 of 24 after 1 min marching slowly on a far goal, with the scaling block 2/true/2/0).
# Every wave, horde and roamer top-up reads the players and their gear (Chaos counted, IncludeAdmins true), so the span
# measures the reads inside the real tick. About 12 min after the first health line with 50 or more tracked, every event
# is stopped; the orchestrator runs `pwsh tools/preflight.ps1 -TimingSpan <log copy> -Windows 10 -MinTracked 50`.
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with scaling step 3; the five entries above enabled, every other spawning definition disabled;
# [Debug] TimingLog = true; [Scoreboard] IncludeAdmins = true; [General] MaxConcurrentEvents 5 or more (Review 1 F2);
# [UnitWatch] StallMinutes 30 for this run only (the 10-minute backstop would clear the quiet last waves inside the span);
# [Limits] MaxUnitsPerWave 24 or more and MaxTrackedUnits 150; NyarDevTools (.devtp) and DevChatEcho; Chaos invulnerable
# (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 ( timeout=40
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start sc-timing-a
expect-log event sc-timing-a wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start sc-timing-b
expect-log event sc-timing-b wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start sc-timing-c
expect-log event sc-timing-c wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start sc-timing-d
expect-log event sc-timing-d wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling sc-timing-d wave 1: players 1, gear [0-9]+, level [0-9]+, units 12 -> 12
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling apo-test roamers: players 1, per hotspot 10, max 30 timeout=30
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling apo-test horde 1: players 1, gear [0-9]+, level [0-9]+, units 24 -> 24 timeout=120
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<T1>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${T1} >= 50
shot full sc-timing-start
# the measured span starts at the first health line with 50 or more tracked (every 10 min from boot)
expect-seen nyar health: 5 events, ([5-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9][0-9]) tracked timeout=660
wait 360
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<T2>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${T2} >= 50
wait 360
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<T3>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${T3} >= 50
shot full sc-timing-end
chat .nyar event stop sc-timing-a
expect-log event sc-timing-a stopped
chat .nyar event stop sc-timing-b
expect-log event sc-timing-b stopped
chat .nyar event stop sc-timing-c
expect-log event sc-timing-c stopped
chat .nyar event stop sc-timing-d
expect-log event sc-timing-d stopped
chat .nyar event stop apo-test
expect-log event apo-test stopped
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=60
console TPHome
wait 3
